WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:08.040
So picture a crowded market square right in the middle of the 16th century.

00:08.040 --> 00:10.580
Right. Lots of noise, chaos.

00:10.820 --> 00:16.060
Exactly. It's super loud. It smells like wood smoke and, you know, unwashed bodies.

00:16.820 --> 00:23.760
And the cobblestones are just packed with people gathered around this makeshift wooden stage.

00:23.920 --> 00:26.780
A pretty typical scene for traveling actors back then.

00:26.780 --> 00:30.320
Yeah, and they're performing the biblical story of the sacrifice of Isaac.

00:30.840 --> 00:34.480
You know the setup, right? Abraham has his son bound on the altar.

00:34.580 --> 00:35.860
Right. The tension is peaking.

00:36.000 --> 00:38.900
He raises the sacrificial knife high into the air.

00:39.400 --> 00:40.980
This is the absolute climax.

00:41.240 --> 00:48.760
This is the exact moment the angel of the Lord is supposed to burst from behind the curtain, grab Abraham's wrist, and stop the slaughter.

00:49.260 --> 00:51.940
But things don't go according to plan.

00:51.940 --> 00:55.800
No. The actor playing the angel misses his cue.

00:55.800 --> 00:58.260
He is a second and a half late.

00:58.900 --> 01:05.880
And for that one and a half seconds, the actor playing Abraham, who is already in motion, begins to bring the blade down.

01:06.020 --> 01:06.600
Oh, wow.

01:06.940 --> 01:08.580
The script is totally broken.

01:09.040 --> 01:15.680
And in that terrifying interval, this genuine suffocating silence falls over the whole crowd.

01:16.020 --> 01:19.260
And, you know, the historical context there is so vital.

01:19.260 --> 01:24.760
Because in the 16th century, the theological narrative wasn't this perfect monolith.

01:25.260 --> 01:27.400
Right. It wasn't set in stone for everyone.

01:27.580 --> 01:34.280
Exactly. There are these obscure, heretical traditions circulating in the background where the knife actually does fall.

01:34.280 --> 01:41.460
So for that 1.5 seconds, that crowd isn't just watching a theatrical mistake.

01:41.600 --> 01:43.140
They think it might actually happen.

01:43.140 --> 01:56.180
Yeah. They're suspended in this raw, unmediated terror that the physical reality unfolding in front of them might permanently deviate from the safe script they expected.

01:56.460 --> 01:58.140
That is so intense.

01:58.140 --> 02:08.120
It really is. They are suddenly forced to live in the gap between the story they were promised and the terrifying physical movement of that blade.

02:08.340 --> 02:18.360
And when the angel finally stumbles onto the stage and the ram is substituted, the relief that washes over the audience isn't because they thought a literal murder was taking place.

02:18.380 --> 02:19.420
Right. It's something deeper.

02:19.420 --> 02:22.400
It's the relief of the narrative being restored.

02:23.000 --> 02:26.020
I mean, we are desperate for the script to hold together.

02:26.460 --> 02:36.920
And that desperate human need to cling to structure, even when reality is constantly breaking our scripts, that is the beating heart of what we are unpacking today.

02:37.060 --> 02:38.320
I'm so excited for this one.

02:38.360 --> 02:38.820
Me too.

02:38.820 --> 02:46.420
We are doing a deep dive into a truly strange, mesmerizing screenplay titled City of Brutes.

02:46.420 --> 02:49.360
It's by an independent researcher named Fliction.

02:49.800 --> 02:53.860
And it is definitely not your standard three-act Hollywood movie.

02:53.940 --> 02:54.680
Not at all.

02:55.140 --> 03:04.800
It presents itself as this event history, basically a chronicle of a massive institutional machine collapsing under the weight of its own information.

03:05.080 --> 03:13.560
And our guide through this whole collapse is a real historical 16th century diplomat named Girolamo Rorario.

03:13.560 --> 03:14.160
Yes.

03:14.460 --> 03:19.560
Rorario is fascinated because he is a man entirely defined by the human systems of order.

03:19.740 --> 03:22.620
You know, diplomacy, language, treaties, bureaucracy.

03:23.020 --> 03:28.560
But after decades of navigating this system, he arrives at a really singular, provocative hypothesis.

03:29.400 --> 03:29.540
Right.

03:29.620 --> 03:31.460
He writes this whole treatise in Latin.

03:31.720 --> 03:32.300
He does.

03:32.380 --> 03:32.560
Yeah.

03:32.880 --> 03:37.000
Quod animalia bruta rationi utantur mellius homine.

03:37.720 --> 03:39.380
Which translates to...

03:39.380 --> 03:42.840
That brute animals employ reason better than man.

03:42.840 --> 03:43.400
Exactly.

03:44.120 --> 03:46.840
Which, you know, sounds like a provocation.

03:47.060 --> 03:47.360
Yeah.

03:47.600 --> 03:49.920
Or maybe a piece of philosophical satire.

03:50.180 --> 03:54.220
But Fliction's text treats it as a devastatingly sincere conclusion.

03:55.060 --> 04:01.900
The screenplay forces us to follow Rorario as he maps out the boundaries of three overlapping domains of existence.

04:02.320 --> 04:05.500
And those three domains really structure the whole journey.

04:05.500 --> 04:06.060
Yeah.

04:06.440 --> 04:13.520
We are going to look at the administrative domain, which is the labyrinth of human bureaucracy and language.

04:13.920 --> 04:16.840
Then we are going to contrast that with the animal domain.

04:17.060 --> 04:17.340
Right.

04:17.440 --> 04:22.900
Which operates in a state of pure, unmediated physical reality.

04:22.900 --> 04:35.960
And finally, we will look at the performative domain, which is basically how humans use theater like that moment with the falling knife to cope when our administrative maps completely fail to match the physical territory.

04:35.960 --> 04:39.540
And the destination of this text is profound.

04:40.620 --> 04:49.680
We are tracking how a lifetime of chaotic, bleeding, contradictory reality eventually gets fed into the machinery of human history.

04:49.680 --> 04:51.160
It's a brutal process.

04:51.600 --> 04:52.300
It really is.

04:52.840 --> 05:06.180
Fliction shows us the compression algorithm of history, where an entire sprawling universe of lived truth gets flattened down into exactly 11 lines of an encyclopedia entry.

05:06.520 --> 05:07.480
11 lines.

05:07.720 --> 05:09.740
It gives me chills just thinking about it.

05:10.240 --> 05:17.840
But to understand how we end up in that compressed, lifeless entry, we have to start at the opposite end of the spectrum.

05:17.840 --> 05:20.900
We have to look at the system operating at peak complexity.

05:21.200 --> 05:21.640
Exactly.

05:22.240 --> 05:25.200
Fliction drops us into state EO.

05:25.500 --> 05:30.480
It's the human domain at the absolute zenith of its illusion of order.

05:31.080 --> 05:34.540
We are in a diplomatic antechamber in the early hours of the morning.

05:35.060 --> 05:39.660
And the text uses this brilliant phrase to describe the acoustic environment.

05:40.420 --> 05:43.480
It says it is operating at maximum channel density.

05:43.920 --> 05:45.140
Maximum channel density.

05:45.440 --> 05:47.580
Just think about the physics of that room for a second.

05:47.580 --> 05:48.900
And it's not a shouting match.

05:48.900 --> 05:49.600
No, no.

05:49.760 --> 05:54.800
Maximum channel density implies that every available frequency of communication is saturated.

05:55.320 --> 05:59.300
There are dozens of conversations happening simultaneously, overlapping.

05:59.580 --> 06:04.240
Just creating this ambient hum of distributed geopolitical processing.

06:04.660 --> 06:04.960
Right.

06:05.580 --> 06:11.280
But the visual architecture of the room completely undermines this feeling of power.

06:11.940 --> 06:15.120
The walls are defined by a negative cartography.

06:15.120 --> 06:18.040
Oh man, I found that detail so haunting.

06:18.440 --> 06:22.660
The plaster walls are covered in these faint rectangular discolorations.

06:22.880 --> 06:23.160
Yes.

06:23.940 --> 06:29.580
Pale spots where massive tapestries or portraits of monarchs or certificates of authority used

06:29.580 --> 06:30.020
to hang.

06:30.240 --> 06:31.460
But they've all been removed.

06:32.200 --> 06:36.860
It establishes the entire epistemological baseline of the human system.

06:36.860 --> 06:37.640
How so?

06:37.640 --> 06:43.480
Well, the people in this room are making decisions that supposedly shape the world, right?

06:44.120 --> 06:50.420
But they are doing so in a space where the objective symbols of authority have literally faded

06:50.420 --> 06:52.060
into negative space.

06:52.180 --> 06:54.060
They are operating on ghost authority.

06:54.180 --> 06:54.640
Exactly.

06:55.240 --> 06:59.600
The framework that justifies their endless talking has already been subtracted from the

06:59.600 --> 07:00.040
environment.

07:00.860 --> 07:05.320
And fliction gives us a microscopic view of how that talking actually functions.

07:05.320 --> 07:07.700
With the two diplomats at the far end of the room.

07:07.840 --> 07:08.020
Yeah.

07:08.300 --> 07:10.120
They are standing perfectly still.

07:10.520 --> 07:12.520
Their voices are measured and collegial.

07:12.720 --> 07:17.320
But they are locked in a total adversarial death spiral.

07:17.560 --> 07:19.020
It's so passive aggressive.

07:19.700 --> 07:20.020
Totally.

07:20.480 --> 07:22.100
The first diplomat states,

07:22.420 --> 07:24.140
The courier departed before dawn.

07:24.520 --> 07:25.720
The road was clear.

07:26.480 --> 07:28.520
Then there is this calculated pause.

07:28.640 --> 07:30.200
And the second diplomat responds,

07:30.960 --> 07:32.560
That is not what we were told.

07:32.560 --> 07:33.060
Right.

07:33.280 --> 07:37.020
And the precision of the phrasing is the key to the dysfunction.

07:37.620 --> 07:42.160
What's fascinating here is that he doesn't actually accuse the first guy of lying.

07:42.980 --> 07:46.400
He redirects the friction to the system of reporting itself.

07:46.580 --> 07:46.840
Yes.

07:46.980 --> 07:49.420
So the first diplomat counters with,

07:49.560 --> 07:51.780
The report you received was compiled yesterday.

07:52.240 --> 07:53.960
And the second parries with,

07:54.040 --> 07:56.400
The report I received was subsequently revised.

07:56.700 --> 07:59.880
They are trapped in a complete deadlock of reality.

07:59.880 --> 08:03.900
One asserts X is the absolute truth.

08:04.100 --> 08:06.300
The other asserts Y is the absolute truth.

08:06.540 --> 08:08.160
But neither of them breaks character.

08:08.560 --> 08:11.360
Neither of them stops to demand evidence or,

08:11.460 --> 08:11.820
You know,

08:11.960 --> 08:15.880
Investigate the actual physical reality of the courier on the dirt road.

08:16.280 --> 08:19.800
They grant each other this bizarre provisional validity.

08:20.560 --> 08:23.920
They essentially agree to pretend the contradiction doesn't exist,

08:24.100 --> 08:26.640
So the gears of the conversation can keep turning.

08:26.640 --> 08:32.320
In systems theory, we distinguish between local coherence and global incoherence.

08:32.680 --> 08:36.340
Locally, within the microscopic grammar of their exchange,

08:36.840 --> 08:38.360
They are perfectly coherent.

08:38.620 --> 08:38.920
Right.

08:39.080 --> 08:41.120
They are observing the rules of etiquette.

08:41.220 --> 08:43.060
They are matching each other's cadence.

08:43.700 --> 08:45.140
The syntax is flawless.

08:45.840 --> 08:52.000
But globally, in terms of the actual physical truth of the world they are supposedly managing,

08:52.680 --> 08:54.640
The system is entirely incoherent.

08:54.640 --> 09:00.040
The reality of the courier is completely lost in the linguistic performance.

09:00.260 --> 09:05.520
And that decay of truth happens right in front of our eyes with the translator sequence.

09:05.900 --> 09:10.000
This is a master class in how language actively destroys reality.

09:10.120 --> 09:11.520
Oh, this scene is incredible.

09:11.960 --> 09:16.420
So a voice from off screen, one of the principal negotiators, says,

09:16.420 --> 09:18.700
The terms were accepted in full.

09:19.400 --> 09:25.760
The translator, who is acting as the node between the two parties, takes the input and relays.

09:26.220 --> 09:27.620
The terms are accepted.

09:27.980 --> 09:30.360
And the principal voice instantly corrects him.

09:30.640 --> 09:32.000
He says, in full.

09:32.300 --> 09:35.540
Now, watch the mechanism of the translator's mind here.

09:35.900 --> 09:38.120
He hesitates for exactly two seconds.

09:38.320 --> 09:41.580
That is the latency period of human linguistic calculation.

09:41.580 --> 09:51.980
He is weighing the social friction of the absolute phrase in full against the diplomatic necessity of moving the conversation forward.

09:52.540 --> 09:52.680
Right.

09:52.680 --> 09:55.520
And he outputs a semantic displacement.

09:56.200 --> 10:00.040
He relays the terms were accepted without registered objection.

10:00.240 --> 10:02.240
It's a total downgrade of reality.

10:02.360 --> 10:03.140
It really is.

10:03.140 --> 10:14.820
He takes a robust, positive condition, the active embracing of terms in full, and mathematically converts it into nothing more than the absence of a negative condition.

10:15.020 --> 10:17.860
He strips all the enthusiasm and finality.

10:17.860 --> 10:28.520
And replaces it with a void where an objection just happens to not be present, and the people on the receiving end simply absorb this downgraded reality and proceed.

10:28.920 --> 10:35.700
The entire foundation of their geopolitical treaty has just suffered an irreversible entropy of meaning.

10:36.180 --> 10:38.720
And the system doesn't even register the loss.

10:39.040 --> 10:42.400
Because the system doesn't measure truth, it measures flow.

10:42.400 --> 10:47.940
As long as the language continues to circulate, the administration believes it is functioning.

10:48.540 --> 10:52.300
And we see this manifested physically in the actions of Rororio himself.

10:53.500 --> 10:56.180
He approaches a table covered in state documents.

10:56.600 --> 11:00.480
Operating with what Fliction calls a trained illegibility.

11:00.960 --> 11:01.220
Right.

11:01.600 --> 11:03.680
He is the perfect bureaucratic instrument.

11:03.940 --> 11:05.880
He picks up two documents.

11:06.220 --> 11:08.900
One is a sealed, uncompromised packet.

11:09.440 --> 11:10.900
The other has already been opened.

11:10.900 --> 11:16.440
Its wax is broken, the paper is creased, its secrecy is entirely compromised.

11:16.800 --> 11:18.220
So what does Rororio do?

11:18.680 --> 11:27.800
He takes the compromised document, folds it up, and physically tucks it inside the flaps of the pristine, sealed document.

11:28.020 --> 11:32.100
He presses the edges together so it looks like a single, unified object.

11:32.640 --> 11:34.620
He constructs a composite lie.

11:34.620 --> 11:36.880
Okay, let's unpack this for everyone listening.

11:37.080 --> 11:49.580
Because this feels exactly like a massive corporate email chain where no one agrees, but someone finally replies understood moving forward just to create the illusion of a decision.

11:49.760 --> 11:50.800
That's a great analogy.

11:50.900 --> 11:52.760
Like, think about a digital file wrapper.

11:52.760 --> 11:58.980
If you've ever dealt with a corrupt video file or a broken PDF, you know exactly what Rororio is doing.

11:59.540 --> 12:08.240
The outer file format, like the .pdf extension, tells the computer's operating system, I am a healthy, functioning file.

12:08.400 --> 12:12.900
And the operating system reads the header, believes the lie, and moves the file around.

12:13.000 --> 12:14.760
You can email it, you can upload it.

12:15.080 --> 12:16.560
The system is perfectly happy.

12:16.560 --> 12:17.560
Exactly.

12:18.280 --> 12:25.560
But the payload inside, the actual code of the video, is a garbled mess of broken pixels and dead audio.

12:26.560 --> 12:34.360
The system remains blissfully ignorant right up until the exact moment a human being actually clicks on it and tries to open it.

12:34.480 --> 12:36.800
At which point the entire application crashes.

12:37.300 --> 12:37.660
Yes.

12:38.440 --> 12:42.680
Rororio is wrapping corrupt data in a healthy file extension.

12:42.680 --> 12:47.400
How does a system like this not just instantly collapse?

12:47.820 --> 12:52.120
Well, the system persists because it produces locally adequate responses.

12:53.400 --> 12:57.480
The state machinery, like the operating system, only reads the headers.

12:58.060 --> 13:04.140
It doesn't have the processing power to constantly open every single document and verify global coherence.

13:04.260 --> 13:07.860
It relies entirely on the local coherence of the wax seal.

13:07.980 --> 13:08.440
Exactly.

13:08.840 --> 13:10.160
Rororio isn't failing.

13:10.160 --> 13:16.000
He is adapting to the only metric the system actually rewards, the appearance of continuity.

13:16.280 --> 13:20.020
But the cognitive cost of maintaining that appearance is just catastrophic.

13:20.760 --> 13:28.900
Humans are constantly lagging behind the actual physical present because everything we do has to be routed through this clumsy machinery of language.

13:29.040 --> 13:31.480
Which brings us to the core contrast of the text.

13:31.840 --> 13:32.140
Right.

13:32.140 --> 13:39.440
If human cognition is defined by this agonizing lag, what happens if we strip away the language entirely?

13:40.000 --> 13:43.840
What does a zero-lag interaction with reality look like?

13:43.940 --> 13:47.400
And that question violently pulls the film into its second domain.

13:48.680 --> 13:49.340
The animal.

13:49.700 --> 13:51.400
This shift in focus is jarring.

13:52.140 --> 13:57.120
We leave the acoustic hum of the diplomats and are thrown into a stable courtyard.

13:57.120 --> 14:04.420
A farrier is working on a horse, rasping the hoof of its right front leg, which he holds clamped between his knees.

14:04.620 --> 14:13.320
So the horse is forced to balance its massive weight on three legs, while a human being actively applies shifting physical pressure to the fourth.

14:13.460 --> 14:18.560
And fliction directs the camera's attention strictly to the horse's musculature and weight distribution.

14:18.560 --> 14:23.200
The biological reality here is astounding.

14:23.860 --> 14:32.020
The text notes that the horse is making thousands of continuous microscopic adjustments across the muscles of its three grounded legs.

14:32.160 --> 14:41.340
It is dynamically compensating for the erratic movements of the farrier, the unevenness of the cobblestones, and the creeping fatigue in its own tendons.

14:41.340 --> 14:46.420
But the critical philosophical observation here is the mechanism of that compensation.

14:46.420 --> 14:49.300
There is absolutely no deliberation.

14:49.800 --> 14:50.000
Right.

14:50.180 --> 14:54.160
It doesn't pause to hold a committee meeting about its center of gravity.

14:54.360 --> 14:54.960
Precisely.

14:55.380 --> 14:58.340
It is operating entirely on proprioception.

14:59.220 --> 15:04.440
Proprioception is basically the body's ability to sense its movement, action, and location.

15:05.120 --> 15:14.500
In a complex animal like a horse, the sensory receptors in the muscles and joints are feeding data directly to the spinal cord.

15:14.500 --> 15:22.300
Which sends motor commands right back out to the muscles, bypassing the executive decision-making centers of the brain entirely.

15:23.000 --> 15:25.760
The horse doesn't possess the capacity to hesitate.

15:26.060 --> 15:29.680
Because hesitation requires a space between input and output.

15:30.260 --> 15:32.380
A space where you evaluate alternatives.

15:32.920 --> 15:38.200
But the horse simply negotiates with gravity in continuous unmediated real time.

15:38.840 --> 15:42.440
And Morerio literally stops in the courtyard to watch this.

15:42.440 --> 15:50.700
He sees a creature executing an incredibly complex physical problem without suffering the pause of self-assessment.

15:51.160 --> 15:52.260
He sees perfection.

15:52.920 --> 15:58.760
And we see that perfection contrasted directly with human failure on the roads of post-Mohawks Hungary.

15:58.920 --> 16:01.140
Oh, this scene is so frustrating to watch.

16:01.500 --> 16:01.960
It is.

16:01.960 --> 16:06.180
The geopolitical map of this region has been shattered by war.

16:06.860 --> 16:07.880
The borders are fluid.

16:08.060 --> 16:09.740
The old landmarks are destroyed.

16:10.340 --> 16:13.320
We watch a human rider traveling down a dirt road.

16:13.840 --> 16:16.180
And he moves in a state of constant paralysis.

16:16.900 --> 16:23.680
He rides 10 yards, halts, pulls out a parchment map, stares at the road, stares at the map.

16:23.680 --> 16:30.020
He realizes the human representation of the terrain no longer matches the physical terrain.

16:30.360 --> 16:35.060
Gets flustered, puts the map away, rides another 10 yards, and halts again.

16:35.160 --> 16:38.820
His cognitive software is trapped in an infinite loading loop.

16:39.180 --> 16:40.140
The map is broken.

16:40.740 --> 16:44.060
And therefore his physical ability to move through the world is broken.

16:44.400 --> 16:48.980
Now sharing the exact same frame, moving down the exact same politically damaged road,

16:49.400 --> 16:52.380
is a pair of oxen pulling a heavy wooden cart.

16:52.380 --> 16:57.260
They approach a section of the road that has been violently washed out by a flood,

16:57.440 --> 17:00.920
leaving only a narrow, precarious strip of stable dirt.

17:01.240 --> 17:07.080
The human rider would have stopped, consulted a surveyor, and written a request for an infrastructure grant.

17:07.120 --> 17:08.600
But what do the oxen do?

17:08.920 --> 17:14.460
The lead ox simply feels the loss of resistance on its right hoof where the dirt falls away,

17:14.620 --> 17:21.500
and it instantaneously applies a continuous graded leftward pressure against the heavy wooden yoke.

17:21.500 --> 17:26.840
It redistributes the vector of its pulling force without ever breaking its forward stride.

17:27.720 --> 17:31.940
It treats the damaged reality of the road purely as sensory input,

17:32.200 --> 17:36.580
and its output is a flawless, real-time physical correction.

17:37.540 --> 17:45.300
And, uh, my favorite visual manifestation of this zero-latency existence is the scene with the village girl.

17:45.300 --> 17:46.320
The bubbles.

17:46.680 --> 17:46.980
Yes.

17:47.540 --> 17:50.480
A little girl is blowing soap bubbles into the wind.

17:50.640 --> 17:52.000
Her dog is chasing them.

17:52.460 --> 17:54.280
Think about the physics of a soap bubble.

17:54.640 --> 17:58.340
It is the definition of chaotic, unpredictable movement.

17:58.560 --> 17:59.840
The wind shears it.

18:00.360 --> 18:01.960
The temperature changes its altitude.

18:02.200 --> 18:04.160
It darts in three dimensions erratically.

18:04.160 --> 18:11.060
If you asked a human being to consciously calculate the trajectory of a bubble, the brain would freeze.

18:11.380 --> 18:16.320
You would have to account for fluid dynamics, wind velocity, the mass of the bubble.

18:16.600 --> 18:20.580
But the dog commits its entire physical being to the chase instantly.

18:21.380 --> 18:24.920
It doesn't organize its body toward where the bubble currently is.

18:24.920 --> 18:32.260
It calculates the exact interception point in three-dimensional space where the bubble will be in the next fraction of a second.

18:32.840 --> 18:37.780
The dog's nervous system is a master class in predictive physical modeling.

18:38.300 --> 18:43.300
And the most vital part, the dog completely lacks the emotion of failure.

18:43.660 --> 18:43.960
Right.

18:44.200 --> 18:47.840
Sometimes it snaps its jaws and the bubble boosts on its nose.

18:48.180 --> 18:54.640
Sometimes the wind catches it and the dog bites Envy Bear while the bubble pops on a fence.

18:54.920 --> 18:58.900
The dog doesn't sit down and revise its methodology.

18:59.300 --> 19:02.280
It doesn't feel shame that the village girl saw it miss.

19:03.060 --> 19:07.140
It simply resets its physical geometry and tracks the next bubble.

19:07.300 --> 19:08.740
I have to pause this here, though.

19:09.340 --> 19:14.160
Because I'm looking at this text and I'm looking at your notes on proprioception and zero latency

19:14.160 --> 19:18.420
and I'm finding myself fundamentally irritated by Rorario's premise.

19:18.760 --> 19:19.980
Really? How come?

19:19.980 --> 19:25.200
Well, yes, the dog catching the bubble is a beautiful piece of biological machinery.

19:26.040 --> 19:28.940
Yes, the oxen navigate the mud flawlessly.

19:29.480 --> 19:33.200
But wait, the dog didn't design the yoke the oxen are wearing.

19:33.360 --> 19:33.880
That's true.

19:34.120 --> 19:36.960
The horse didn't pave the cobblestone courtyard.

19:38.020 --> 19:41.580
Lag is the biological price we pay for abstraction.

19:41.580 --> 19:47.740
Without the linguistic pause, without the ability to step out of the present moment and say,

19:48.020 --> 19:49.620
what if the road was better?

19:51.200 --> 19:53.660
We wouldn't build the carts in the first place.

19:53.940 --> 19:56.680
The humanists of the time would agree with you completely.

19:56.680 --> 20:04.400
Right. So isn't the human cognitive framework, with all its chaotic latency, objectively superior

20:04.400 --> 20:10.060
because it can scale across time and space, whereas the animal is trapped entirely in the

20:10.060 --> 20:11.560
tyranny of the present second?

20:11.840 --> 20:15.220
That is the exact counter-argument they would have deployed.

20:15.680 --> 20:21.980
They argue that reason is defined by the ability to conceive of the universal, not just react

20:21.980 --> 20:22.660
to the particular.

20:22.660 --> 20:28.240
But Fliction's text is suggesting something far darker about the trajectory of human abstraction.

20:28.620 --> 20:29.160
What's that?

20:29.620 --> 20:33.580
Rorario isn't arguing that the dog should be designing aqueducts.

20:33.900 --> 20:35.840
He's pointing out a difference in latency.

20:36.580 --> 20:42.440
He's observing a system where the human capacity for abstraction has reached a terminal point of

20:42.440 --> 20:43.560
diminishing returns.

20:43.560 --> 20:49.860
So our cognitive software, the abstraction that built the world, has basically become legacy

20:49.860 --> 20:52.640
code that is now actively choking the system.

20:53.080 --> 20:53.720
Exactly.

20:54.500 --> 21:01.100
The human ability to model the world through language allowed us to conquer the environment.

21:02.060 --> 21:09.180
But we have now generated so much language, so many maps, so many treaties, that the environment

21:09.180 --> 21:13.340
we must navigate is no longer the physical dirt road.

21:13.340 --> 21:15.720
It is the labyrinth of our own language.

21:15.860 --> 21:16.180
Yes.

21:17.060 --> 21:21.780
The latency was an evolutionary advantage when we were figuring out how to build a fire.

21:21.780 --> 21:27.900
But when you were trapped in a room of 50 men debating the semantic difference between

21:27.900 --> 21:34.520
two Latin verbs while the actual empire crumbles outside, that latency becomes a fatal disease.

21:34.520 --> 21:44.380
The animals are vastly superior reasoners in this text because their method of engaging with reality never produces an error that paralyzes their survival.

21:44.540 --> 21:50.200
Which perfectly sets up the disaster of Section 3, information overload and the breakdown of language.

21:50.200 --> 21:56.900
Because we get to see what happens when the human brain is finally crushed by the sheer weight of its own abstract legacy code.

21:57.380 --> 21:59.580
Rorario isn't just an observer anymore.

21:59.720 --> 22:00.640
He becomes the victim.

22:00.640 --> 22:06.620
And the inciting incident for this total systemic failure happens at the Diet of Regensburg.

22:07.260 --> 22:12.260
The visual and acoustic scale of this scene is just suffocating.

22:12.740 --> 22:16.240
We are in a massive, vaulted assembly chamber.

22:16.240 --> 22:21.720
It is packed with the highest-ranking diplomats, theologians, and legal scholars in Europe.

22:22.280 --> 22:30.860
And the architecture of the room creates a constant, oppressive, low-frequency reverberation of human voices bouncing off stone.

22:31.120 --> 22:34.560
And what are these titans of human intellect doing?

22:34.740 --> 22:35.960
Are they solving famine?

22:36.620 --> 22:38.040
Are they ending wars?

22:38.040 --> 22:46.720
No, they are attempting to amend a single, specific sentence in a theological document called the Book of Regensburg.

22:47.040 --> 22:52.000
They are trapped in the ultimate linguistic paradox, the trap of infinite precision.

22:52.260 --> 22:59.440
Every single time a theologian introduces a new, qualifying word to make his position mathematically precise,

23:00.060 --> 23:04.520
that new word carries its own historical baggage and multiple interpretations.

23:04.520 --> 23:11.200
Which immediately triggers an objection from the opposing faction, who demand a secondary clause to define the new word.

23:11.840 --> 23:15.020
You are watching a real-time demonstration of semantic gridlock.

23:15.400 --> 23:20.200
The text notes, with cold precision, the document grows without converging.

23:21.060 --> 23:23.400
It's the linguistic equivalent of a fractal.

23:24.140 --> 23:27.520
The closer you zoom in, the more the boundaries fracture and multiply.

23:28.140 --> 23:29.680
You can never reach the bottom.

23:30.200 --> 23:33.680
And while these men are physically sweating over the placement of a comma,

23:33.680 --> 23:39.880
fliction cuts to a microscopic detail in the corner of the heavy wooden window frame.

23:39.880 --> 23:46.220
There is a spider, flawlessly weaving an intricate, mathematically stunning web.

23:46.440 --> 23:48.200
The contrast is devastating.

23:48.820 --> 23:50.680
The spider possesses no blueprint.

23:51.360 --> 23:54.060
It has no conceptual understanding of geometry.

23:54.580 --> 24:02.640
It merely executes a sequence of localized, algorithmic movements moving from anchor point to anchor point, dropping silk.

24:02.640 --> 24:09.460
The perfect global structure of the web emerges entirely as a byproduct of its localized action.

24:09.460 --> 24:21.540
It weaves a masterpiece of functional engineering, while utterly indifferent to the 50 human geniuses 10 feet away who are tearing their own society apart over a verb tense.

24:21.620 --> 24:28.320
And sitting in the middle of this reverberating chamber of failure, Rario's physiology begins to buckle.

24:28.320 --> 24:32.420
The text uses a very specific word for his condition, right?

24:32.840 --> 24:32.980
Yeah.

24:33.160 --> 24:33.760
Saturation.

24:34.240 --> 24:34.520
Yes.

24:34.640 --> 24:37.000
Saturation is a crucial concept here.

24:37.940 --> 24:41.240
It is fundamentally different from fatigue or boredom.

24:41.660 --> 24:46.640
If you are bored, you are seeking stimulation, you want time to accelerate.

24:47.360 --> 24:49.940
Saturation is a state of physical fullness.

24:50.420 --> 24:53.200
The medium can hold no more solvent.

24:53.200 --> 24:57.600
In neuroscience, there is a phenomenon called semantic satiation.

24:58.600 --> 25:10.880
If you stare at a word or repeat a word out loud 50 times in a row, the psychological machinery in your brain that links the sound of the word to its meaning suddenly uncouples.

25:11.240 --> 25:11.520
Right.

25:11.620 --> 25:16.180
You look at the word chair and suddenly it's just a bizarre collection of lines and curves.

25:16.380 --> 25:17.740
It sounds like alien nonsense.

25:17.740 --> 25:24.620
Your brain has fatigued the specific neural pathway of meaning, leaving only the raw sensory input.

25:24.940 --> 25:28.900
That is exactly what Fliction is describing, but scaled up to an entire worldview.

25:29.560 --> 25:36.040
Rario's Wernicke's area, the part of the brain responsible for language comprehension, is overloading.

25:36.320 --> 25:38.040
He hears the diplomat speaking.

25:38.760 --> 25:46.520
The syntax is entering his ear canal, but his brain refuses to elaborate those acoustic waves into semantic meaning.

25:46.520 --> 25:51.700
The cognitive machinery of interpretation simply powers down to protect itself.

25:51.940 --> 26:01.160
And the screenplay gives us an incredible metaphor to understand exactly how Rario is experiencing the world in this saturated state.

26:01.700 --> 26:03.300
The scene of the falcon handler.

26:03.440 --> 26:04.840
Oh, I love this scene.

26:05.400 --> 26:10.480
The handler is walking through a field with a hooded falcon poached on his heavy leather glove.

26:10.480 --> 26:16.940
He's a lonely guy, so he's just chatting away, talking continuously to the bird about his life.

26:17.180 --> 26:20.100
But the falcon doesn't understand human nouns and verbs.

26:20.780 --> 26:23.960
It is reacting purely to the physics of the sound wave.

26:24.160 --> 26:26.460
It is reacting to the prosody.

26:26.780 --> 26:27.700
Right, the prosody.

26:28.080 --> 26:32.900
The volume, the rhythm, the emotional vibration of the handler's vocal cords.

26:32.900 --> 26:40.600
When the handler gets excited and his voice rises in titch, the falcon instinctively tightens its talons on the leather.

26:40.600 --> 26:48.200
When the rhythm of the speak slows down into a calm cadence, the bird relaxes its posture and adjusts its balance.

26:48.700 --> 26:54.780
The falcon is perfectly decoding the physical music of the speech while remaining entirely blind to the lyrics.

26:55.100 --> 27:00.660
And that exact animalistic auditory processing becomes Rororio's reality.

27:00.660 --> 27:03.600
The hollowing out of his intellect is complete.

27:04.500 --> 27:08.520
We see a scene where a female relative visits him in his private study.

27:08.980 --> 27:12.780
It is framed like an intimate, vital family conversation.

27:13.580 --> 27:19.180
But Flixian's narration reveals the horror of Rororio's internal state.

27:19.640 --> 27:24.600
He is experiencing her words exactly as the falcon experiences the handler.

27:24.880 --> 27:25.860
He hears the tone.

27:26.500 --> 27:27.440
He maps the rhythm.

27:27.440 --> 27:37.140
He registers the pauses where a response is socially required, and he outputs a mechanical, locally adequate hum of agreement.

27:37.500 --> 27:45.700
But the actual semantic meaning of what she is telling him about their family, about their shared history, it vanishes into thin air.

27:46.280 --> 27:51.720
He is locked inside his own head, listening to the meaningless music of human vibration.

27:51.720 --> 27:53.800
Language has died inside him.

27:54.280 --> 28:01.560
And this internal death culminates in one of the most chilling, quiet sequences in the entire text, which concludes Day 2.

28:01.960 --> 28:03.000
It is late at night.

28:03.440 --> 28:04.480
The world is dark.

28:04.720 --> 28:09.360
Rororio is sitting alone at his heavy wooden desk, illuminated by a single candle.

28:10.140 --> 28:15.460
He is doing the one thing he has done tens of thousands of times in his life, writing a diplomatic letter.

28:15.460 --> 28:18.120
The physical muscle memory is carrying him.

28:18.400 --> 28:19.880
He writes the formal greeting.

28:20.360 --> 28:24.240
He crafts the ornate subordinate clauses required by protocol.

28:24.580 --> 28:26.520
He's moving down the page effortlessly.

28:27.060 --> 28:30.920
And then, he reaches the structural center of the document.

28:31.700 --> 28:38.560
The exact point where the core claim, the actual vital truth of the message, must be articulated.

28:39.000 --> 28:40.120
And his pen stops.

28:40.120 --> 28:42.440
It stops dead on the parchment.

28:42.880 --> 28:48.700
It rests there long enough that a little pool of black ink bleeds into the fibers of the paper.

28:49.360 --> 28:50.520
He didn't intend to stop.

28:50.900 --> 28:52.440
He isn't physically exhausted.

28:52.620 --> 28:54.000
His hand isn't cramped.

28:54.400 --> 28:59.000
The script notes simply, the continuation has not arrived.

29:00.080 --> 29:05.940
The connection between human intention and linguistic execution has been severed.

29:06.020 --> 29:09.280
It is a total systemic failure of language as a tool.

29:09.280 --> 29:11.640
Here's where it gets really interesting for you listening.

29:12.080 --> 29:15.540
Have you ever stared at a blinking cursor on a blank screen?

29:15.900 --> 29:20.600
You have to write a critical email or maybe a deeply emotional text message.

29:20.740 --> 29:22.940
You know exactly what you feel in your chest.

29:23.000 --> 29:23.240
Yes.

29:23.480 --> 29:25.860
You know the exact reality you want to convey.

29:25.860 --> 29:32.540
But as you stare at the cursor blinking, the cognitive bridge between your internal reality

29:32.540 --> 29:37.120
and the external symbols of the alphabet collapses, your brain just empties.

29:37.200 --> 29:39.060
You aren't experiencing writer's block.

29:39.280 --> 29:44.400
You are experiencing the fundamental inadequacy of language to map human reality.

29:44.400 --> 29:46.240
So what does Rorario do?

29:46.740 --> 29:54.020
He folds the half-finished incomplete letter, seals it with wax, and places it in the outgoing courier pile.

29:54.400 --> 29:57.680
Because the administrative machine cannot process absence.

29:58.180 --> 30:03.600
It requires the physical object of the letter, regardless of whether the letter contains any truth.

30:03.600 --> 30:10.520
And this brings us to the profound sociological question of Section 4, the performative domain.

30:10.520 --> 30:20.440
If language is dead, if our maps are broken and our letters are empty, how does human society avoid tearing itself apart in the resulting chaos?

30:20.440 --> 30:23.680
We abandon truth, and we embrace theater.

30:23.680 --> 30:30.840
If we can no longer agree on the physical reality of the world, we desperately agree to follow a script.

30:31.220 --> 30:38.200
Structural functionalism in sociology dictates that institutions survive not because the individuals inside them are competent,

30:38.660 --> 30:41.940
but because the roles themselves provide a stabilizing architecture.

30:41.940 --> 30:48.820
Right, and Fliction explores this through a series of theatrical performances that mimic humi-institutional behavior.

30:49.540 --> 30:52.800
The most conceptually dense of these is the tavern scene.

30:53.280 --> 30:55.800
I can visualize this scene so vividly.

30:56.240 --> 30:59.280
It's a claustrophobic, smoke-filled tavern.

30:59.280 --> 31:06.480
A group of heavily intoxicated men have pushed two heavy oak tables together to form a crude stage.

31:07.020 --> 31:10.020
They are acting out the story of David and Goliath.

31:10.100 --> 31:11.100
It starts normally.

31:11.400 --> 31:16.140
A massive towering drank steps onto the table and bellows,

31:16.480 --> 31:17.540
I am Goliath.

31:17.980 --> 31:21.840
A smaller, scrappier man steps up opposite him and shouts,

31:21.960 --> 31:23.100
I am David!

31:23.100 --> 31:27.980
They pantomime the swinging of the sling, the stone hitting the giant,

31:28.180 --> 31:31.280
and the massive man crashes onto the wooden table.

31:31.980 --> 31:33.060
The crowd cheers.

31:33.600 --> 31:35.840
It's standard barroom theatrics.

31:36.220 --> 31:38.920
But then the underlying logic of the system begins to mutate.

31:39.400 --> 31:40.560
They reset the scene.

31:41.160 --> 31:43.320
The giant who just played Goliath stands up,

31:43.660 --> 31:45.080
walks to the opposite end of the table,

31:45.200 --> 31:46.200
and boldly announces,

31:46.920 --> 31:47.860
I am David.

31:47.920 --> 31:50.780
And a completely new patron climbs out of the crowd,

31:50.780 --> 31:52.280
steps onto the Goliath side,

31:52.280 --> 31:52.880
and shouts,

31:53.020 --> 31:53.920
I am Goliath!

31:54.020 --> 31:56.700
They are freely swapping the archetypal roles.

31:56.900 --> 31:59.120
And the audience's suspension of disbelief holds.

31:59.860 --> 32:03.080
The crowd instantly accepts that the giant is now the underdog.

32:03.600 --> 32:06.400
The physical reality of the men's bodies doesn't matter.

32:06.840 --> 32:10.880
The only thing that matters is the spatial designation of the role on the table.

32:11.280 --> 32:14.360
But then the system experiences a critical error.

32:15.040 --> 32:17.460
Two men climb onto the stage simultaneously.

32:17.460 --> 32:19.700
They look at each other, look at the crowd,

32:19.840 --> 32:20.900
and both of them shout,

32:21.320 --> 32:22.260
I am David.

32:22.280 --> 32:25.660
The system has generated a duplication error.

32:26.100 --> 32:29.280
The narrative architecture of David and Goliath is binary.

32:30.040 --> 32:32.620
It requires an oppressor and an underdog.

32:33.080 --> 32:35.360
It cannot process two underdogs.

32:35.640 --> 32:38.080
The entire tavern goes dead silent.

32:38.300 --> 32:39.440
The cheering stops.

32:39.620 --> 32:41.720
The crowd is genuinely disturbed,

32:42.000 --> 32:44.040
paralyzed by the collapse of the script.

32:44.600 --> 32:48.020
Nobody knows how to process the reality of two Davids.

32:48.240 --> 32:50.180
The tension is unbearable.

32:50.180 --> 32:52.880
Until, from the very back of the dark tavern,

32:53.400 --> 32:57.280
a voice yells out the most brilliant, horrifying line in the text.

32:57.360 --> 32:59.240
Then one must be Goliath.

32:59.240 --> 33:02.500
It is the ultimate distillation of institutional violence.

33:02.500 --> 33:05.240
The structure of the story demands an enemy.

33:05.240 --> 33:07.580
If two innocent men show up,

33:07.580 --> 33:12.860
the narrative pressure of the system dictates that one of them must be stripped of his identity

33:12.860 --> 33:15.240
and transformed into the monster,

33:15.240 --> 33:18.120
simply to allow the gears of the story to keep turning.

33:18.680 --> 33:21.080
Neither man actually yields the title.

33:21.400 --> 33:22.160
Neither man says,

33:22.320 --> 33:23.480
okay, I'll be Goliath.

33:24.020 --> 33:26.660
But the scene violently resumes anyway.

33:27.560 --> 33:28.480
They collide.

33:28.940 --> 33:30.360
Someone is thrown off the table,

33:30.360 --> 33:31.740
and the crowd cheers,

33:31.920 --> 33:34.900
relieved that the structure survived the contradiction.

33:35.540 --> 33:39.300
We see this every single day in corporate structures and political systems.

33:39.740 --> 33:41.100
The titles remain stable.

33:41.340 --> 33:43.860
The CEO, the villain, the savior, the victim.

33:44.540 --> 33:48.160
But the actual human beings rotating through those roles

33:48.160 --> 33:51.240
are a chaotic, interchangeable mess.

33:51.240 --> 33:56.380
We don't care if the physical reality of the person matches the role,

33:56.380 --> 34:00.380
as long as the narrative arc of our society remains intact.

34:00.560 --> 34:02.720
We are clinging to the puppet strings.

34:03.620 --> 34:05.160
So what does this all mean?

34:05.280 --> 34:07.420
Are we all just sitting in a puppet show,

34:07.660 --> 34:11.900
ignoring the fact that the script doesn't match what's actually happening in front of our eyes?

34:12.140 --> 34:12.660
Absolutely.

34:13.240 --> 34:17.220
Flection makes the puppet string metaphor literal in the very next scene.

34:17.800 --> 34:20.020
We are shown a traveling puppet theater

34:20.020 --> 34:22.260
performing the tragedy of Cain and Abel.

34:22.680 --> 34:26.060
This scene perfectly isolates the cognitive dissonance

34:26.060 --> 34:28.240
required to live in human society.

34:28.240 --> 34:30.100
The setup is crucial.

34:30.740 --> 34:34.780
There is a narrator standing physically outside the wooden puppet booth.

34:35.740 --> 34:39.420
He is speaking the authoritative script out loud for the audience.

34:39.860 --> 34:43.880
He intones the elder brother brought the offering that was not accepted.

34:44.180 --> 34:47.140
But inside the booth, on the miniature stage,

34:47.520 --> 34:49.980
the physical puppet, representing Cain,

34:50.560 --> 34:53.240
places his tiny wooden offering on the altar.

34:53.240 --> 34:55.060
And it stays perfectly upright.

34:55.180 --> 34:56.980
It looks completely fine.

34:57.560 --> 34:59.820
Then the narrator continues with his script.

35:00.240 --> 35:02.420
The younger brother brought that which was favored.

35:03.020 --> 35:04.320
But as he says this,

35:04.560 --> 35:06.620
the puppet for Abel drops his offering.

35:07.900 --> 35:10.620
The little wooden prop literally breaks in half

35:10.620 --> 35:12.840
and tumbles off the stage into the dirt.

35:13.560 --> 35:16.280
It is a mechanical failure of the puppeteer.

35:16.280 --> 35:17.660
So you have a total schism.

35:17.660 --> 35:21.520
The spoken, authoritative narrative tells you Abel is favored

35:21.520 --> 35:22.800
and Cain is rejected.

35:23.520 --> 35:27.940
But the physical, optical reality happening inches from your face

35:27.940 --> 35:29.880
shows you the exact opposite.

35:30.100 --> 35:31.500
Cain's offering is solid.

35:31.900 --> 35:33.060
And Abel's is shattered.

35:33.640 --> 35:37.640
And how does the human audience react to this irreconcilable contradiction?

35:37.640 --> 35:39.020
The text notes,

35:39.020 --> 35:42.680
the audience attends to both without the performance providing guidance

35:42.680 --> 35:45.520
about which constitutes the authoritative account.

35:45.940 --> 35:46.540
They don't riot.

35:46.980 --> 35:49.440
They don't yell at the narrator to fix the puppets.

35:49.700 --> 35:52.560
They just sit there peacefully absorbing

35:52.560 --> 35:56.380
two mutually exclusive realities simultaneously.

35:56.380 --> 35:59.840
They listen to the official narrative of the world.

36:00.120 --> 36:02.720
They watch the broken physical reality of the world.

36:02.840 --> 36:05.660
And they never once demand that the two align.

36:06.040 --> 36:09.360
Because demanding alignment requires the energy of revolution.

36:10.020 --> 36:13.680
It is vastly easier metabolically and socially

36:13.680 --> 36:16.540
to simply accept the cognitive dissonance.

36:16.960 --> 36:19.940
We hold the map of how the justice system

36:19.940 --> 36:22.920
or the economy is supposedly functioning in one hand

36:22.920 --> 36:27.360
while walking through a physical territory that entirely refutes it.

36:27.560 --> 36:29.280
Which brings us to Section 5,

36:29.800 --> 36:31.120
the geography of ambiguity.

36:31.800 --> 36:34.400
The disconnect between the map and the territory

36:34.400 --> 36:36.420
stops being a psychological metaphor

36:36.420 --> 36:39.360
and becomes the literal physical earth

36:39.360 --> 36:41.260
Rorario has to walk on.

36:41.260 --> 36:44.660
We return to Rorario in his administrative capacity,

36:45.060 --> 36:46.660
standing in a cartographic room.

36:47.200 --> 36:50.040
He is examining a massive, sprawling map

36:50.040 --> 36:51.720
of a contested border region.

36:51.720 --> 36:54.340
But the map is a Frankenstein monster.

36:54.880 --> 36:56.860
It has been patched together over decades

36:56.860 --> 36:59.080
using different types of vellum and paper

36:59.080 --> 37:01.120
drawn by different surveyors

37:01.120 --> 37:03.140
using different mathematical projections.

37:03.820 --> 37:06.100
The physical borders drawn in ink

37:06.100 --> 37:08.740
literally do not line up at the seams.

37:09.340 --> 37:12.380
A heavy black line representing a boundary

37:12.380 --> 37:15.040
comes to the edge of one piece of paper

37:15.040 --> 37:18.980
and the continuation of that exact same line

37:18.980 --> 37:21.000
on the glued adjacent paper

37:21.000 --> 37:23.440
is shifted half an inch to the south.

37:23.440 --> 37:25.540
The human attempt to map the world

37:25.540 --> 37:28.500
has created literal rifts in space.

37:29.560 --> 37:32.780
And the clerk asks Rorario to place a brass marker

37:32.780 --> 37:35.140
on the map to designate a specific,

37:35.320 --> 37:37.180
vital military coordinate.

37:37.440 --> 37:39.560
Rorario's hand hovers over the map.

37:40.200 --> 37:41.580
And where does he place the marker?

37:42.060 --> 37:44.300
He places it directly into the blank,

37:44.440 --> 37:47.800
unresolvable interval between the two mismatched borderlines.

37:47.800 --> 37:50.600
He drops the pin into the error itself.

37:50.880 --> 37:52.460
And the clerk, without batting an eye,

37:52.680 --> 37:54.460
writes down the mathematical coordinates

37:54.460 --> 37:57.100
of that purely fictional impossible location.

37:57.680 --> 38:00.720
He invents a false certainty out of thin air.

38:01.420 --> 38:03.140
That coordinate will be filed away,

38:03.500 --> 38:04.600
copied into treaties,

38:05.140 --> 38:06.700
and men will likely die

38:06.700 --> 38:08.500
trying to defend a piece of geometry

38:08.500 --> 38:11.180
that only exists because two pieces of paper

38:11.180 --> 38:12.580
were glued together poorly.

38:12.580 --> 38:15.000
Infliction then pulls the camera back

38:15.000 --> 38:17.420
to show us what this cartographic insanity

38:17.420 --> 38:21.120
looks like in the actual physical biosphere.

38:21.680 --> 38:25.460
We move to the boundary zone itself at dusk.

38:25.460 --> 38:26.600
Over the years,

38:27.140 --> 38:29.020
different teams of human surveyors

38:29.020 --> 38:31.280
armed with these contradictory maps

38:31.280 --> 38:33.580
have marched out into the fields

38:33.580 --> 38:36.760
and driven heavy wooden stakes into the soil,

38:37.440 --> 38:39.640
claiming the same overlapping territory

38:39.640 --> 38:41.060
for different jurisdictions.

38:41.060 --> 38:42.960
Infliction gives us a detail here

38:42.960 --> 38:44.700
that genuinely blew my mind.

38:45.460 --> 38:46.960
The human fictions have actually

38:46.960 --> 38:48.840
warped to the biology of the earth.

38:49.520 --> 38:51.280
The text describes how the grass

38:51.280 --> 38:52.740
literally grows differently

38:52.740 --> 38:55.760
on either side of these invisible, conflicting lines.

38:56.460 --> 38:57.780
It is a stunning observation

38:57.780 --> 39:00.060
of how belief alters reality.

39:01.240 --> 39:04.020
The local peasants living in this ambiguous zone

39:04.020 --> 39:05.180
follow different laws

39:05.180 --> 39:08.080
depending on which imaginary line they believe in.

39:08.080 --> 39:10.060
One group believes the land belongs

39:10.060 --> 39:12.480
to a jurisdiction that taxes wheat heavily

39:12.480 --> 39:14.220
so they run sheep on it

39:14.220 --> 39:16.420
keeping the grass chewed down to the roots.

39:17.120 --> 39:18.420
The other group believes it belongs

39:18.420 --> 39:21.040
to a jurisdiction that mandates fallow fields

39:21.040 --> 39:23.240
so the grass grows wild and tall.

39:23.480 --> 39:26.480
The pure fiction of the bureaucratic map

39:26.480 --> 39:28.300
has sculpted the physical botany

39:28.300 --> 39:28.980
of the landscape.

39:29.820 --> 39:33.480
It's a landscape of pure human-generated ambiguity.

39:33.480 --> 39:35.980
And it is right in the middle

39:35.980 --> 39:39.460
of this suffocating, overlapping human gridlock

39:39.460 --> 39:42.140
that we are given the ultimate contrast

39:42.140 --> 39:43.640
with the animal domain.

39:44.160 --> 39:45.720
We get the scene of the narrow gate.

39:46.600 --> 39:49.560
Picture a massive, ancient stone archway

39:49.560 --> 39:51.100
leading into a town.

39:51.820 --> 39:53.560
The passage is incredibly tight,

39:53.860 --> 39:56.520
barely wide enough for a single wooden cart

39:56.520 --> 39:59.120
to pass through without scraping the stone.

39:59.120 --> 40:02.880
Two human drivers approaching from opposite directions

40:02.880 --> 40:05.020
meet exactly in the center of the archway.

40:05.940 --> 40:07.720
Now, they don't break out into violence.

40:07.980 --> 40:10.120
Instead, they deploy the very thing

40:10.120 --> 40:12.840
that makes them human-complex social language.

40:13.180 --> 40:14.300
They stop their carts

40:14.300 --> 40:16.800
and engage in an agonizingly polite,

40:17.160 --> 40:19.580
endlessly recursive verbal negotiation.

40:20.400 --> 40:21.160
Oh, I apologize.

40:21.360 --> 40:22.500
I can back my horses up

40:22.500 --> 40:23.900
if you cut your wheel to the left.

40:24.020 --> 40:24.960
No, no, good sir.

40:25.040 --> 40:26.280
The incline is behind me.

40:26.280 --> 40:28.140
If you merely angle your axle,

40:28.520 --> 40:29.980
they are completely paralyzed

40:29.980 --> 40:32.480
by courtesy, social hierarchy,

40:32.840 --> 40:34.680
and the calculation of spatial variables

40:34.680 --> 40:35.680
through language.

40:36.080 --> 40:37.620
They are frozen in a gridlock

40:37.620 --> 40:39.360
of their own cognitive lag.

40:39.960 --> 40:41.480
And while they are talking in circles,

40:41.980 --> 40:43.600
a young boy is standing nearby,

40:44.040 --> 40:46.040
holding a mutt on a leather leash.

40:46.420 --> 40:48.860
The dog looks at the tangled carts,

40:49.460 --> 40:51.240
looks at the narrow, jagged gap

40:51.240 --> 40:52.680
between the wooden wheels

40:52.680 --> 40:55.060
and the stone wall, and acts.

40:55.060 --> 40:57.280
The dog doesn't ask for permission.

40:58.300 --> 41:00.180
It doesn't assess the social standing

41:00.180 --> 41:01.140
of the cart drivers.

41:01.740 --> 41:03.560
It simply pulls its head backward,

41:04.220 --> 41:05.520
slipping the leather collar

41:05.520 --> 41:07.240
smoothly over its ears.

41:07.560 --> 41:09.680
It frees itself from the human constraint,

41:10.160 --> 41:11.520
and with zero hesitation,

41:11.800 --> 41:14.120
the dog perfectly angles its shoulders,

41:14.640 --> 41:16.160
contorts its spine to match

41:16.160 --> 41:18.280
the exact negative space of the gap,

41:18.440 --> 41:20.020
and flows through the wreckage

41:20.020 --> 41:20.820
to the other side.

41:20.820 --> 41:23.120
It continues trotting down the road,

41:23.580 --> 41:25.560
leaving the humans completely trapped

41:25.560 --> 41:27.600
in their endless static negotiation.

41:28.500 --> 41:30.840
The animal solves the physical reality,

41:31.100 --> 41:32.420
while the humans drown

41:32.420 --> 41:33.920
in the social reality.

41:34.320 --> 41:36.000
But Fliction makes sure to emphasize

41:36.000 --> 41:37.220
that animal perception

41:37.220 --> 41:39.460
isn't just about slipping through gaps.

41:39.940 --> 41:41.300
Sometimes the animal's

41:41.300 --> 41:43.320
unmediated connection to reality

41:43.320 --> 41:45.340
tells it to stop entirely,

41:45.740 --> 41:48.000
in direct defiance of human systems.

41:48.000 --> 41:49.660
This is the sequence

41:49.660 --> 41:51.220
of the refusal of the bridge.

41:51.680 --> 41:53.860
Rorario and a diplomatic envoy

41:53.860 --> 41:55.240
are traveling on horseback.

41:55.720 --> 41:58.320
They approach an old heavy stone bridge

41:58.320 --> 42:00.120
spanning a fast-moving river.

42:00.320 --> 42:01.540
The human map says,

42:01.800 --> 42:02.700
here's a bridge.

42:03.380 --> 42:04.740
Bridges are infrastructure

42:04.740 --> 42:06.000
designed to be crossed.

42:06.720 --> 42:08.100
The human brain operating

42:08.100 --> 42:09.120
on that abstraction

42:09.120 --> 42:11.260
commands the body to ride forward.

42:11.780 --> 42:14.020
But the lead horse stops dead.

42:14.320 --> 42:15.820
The rider applies the spurs.

42:15.820 --> 42:17.780
He kicks the horse's flanks,

42:18.240 --> 42:18.900
yanks the bit,

42:19.180 --> 42:20.160
demanding compliance

42:20.160 --> 42:22.180
based on his abstract assumption

42:22.180 --> 42:23.620
that the bridge is safe.

42:23.780 --> 42:24.820
But the horse's proprioceptive

42:25.500 --> 42:26.640
and sensory systems

42:26.640 --> 42:28.620
are processing the physical reality

42:28.620 --> 42:29.800
at a massive bandwidth.

42:30.680 --> 42:32.060
The text specifies

42:32.060 --> 42:33.480
what the horse is registering,

42:34.100 --> 42:36.020
the microscopic shifts in the mortar,

42:36.560 --> 42:37.820
the subtle acoustic reverberation

42:38.420 --> 42:39.720
of the rushing water

42:39.720 --> 42:41.320
against a compromised piling,

42:41.900 --> 42:43.980
a slight unnatural depression

42:43.980 --> 42:44.860
in the roadbed.

42:44.860 --> 42:47.840
The animal registers structural death

42:47.840 --> 42:49.780
and it holds its ground

42:49.780 --> 42:50.660
against the violence

42:50.660 --> 42:51.560
of the human rider.

42:52.180 --> 42:53.620
It absolutely refuses

42:53.620 --> 42:54.980
to step onto the stone.

42:55.220 --> 42:57.340
Eventually, the humiliated humans

42:57.340 --> 42:58.900
give up, turn around,

42:59.120 --> 43:00.340
and spend hours

43:00.340 --> 43:01.740
fording the freezing river

43:01.740 --> 43:02.820
miles downstream.

43:03.540 --> 43:05.000
And then Fliction executes

43:05.000 --> 43:06.020
a brilliant piece

43:06.020 --> 43:07.160
of cinematic timing.

43:07.600 --> 43:08.320
Hours later,

43:08.680 --> 43:10.120
while the humans are shivering

43:10.120 --> 43:11.180
on the far bank

43:11.180 --> 43:12.640
completely off screen,

43:12.640 --> 43:14.520
we just hear a sound.

43:15.140 --> 43:17.400
A massive, echoing,

43:17.560 --> 43:18.600
guttural rumble

43:18.600 --> 43:20.120
of collapsing stone.

43:20.120 --> 43:21.920
The bridge falls into the river

43:21.920 --> 43:22.960
under its own weight.

43:23.640 --> 43:25.160
The horse's zero-latency

43:25.160 --> 43:26.480
perception of reality

43:26.480 --> 43:27.920
was flawlessly accurate,

43:28.420 --> 43:29.740
while the human assumption

43:29.740 --> 43:31.180
of permanent infrastructure

43:31.180 --> 43:33.360
was a deadly fiction.

43:33.360 --> 43:35.320
We've spent this entire time

43:35.320 --> 43:36.940
immersed in the mud,

43:37.060 --> 43:37.460
the blood,

43:37.580 --> 43:38.120
the chaos,

43:38.240 --> 43:38.900
and the vibrant,

43:39.140 --> 43:40.180
terrified reality

43:40.180 --> 43:41.480
of Rorio's life.

43:41.920 --> 43:42.820
We've felt the pen

43:42.820 --> 43:43.760
stop on the paper.

43:44.280 --> 43:45.440
We've watched the dog

43:45.440 --> 43:46.280
catch the bubble.

43:46.640 --> 43:47.740
We've seen the grass

43:47.740 --> 43:49.600
warped by imaginary maps.

43:49.700 --> 43:50.720
This is the mess

43:50.720 --> 43:52.120
of actual existence.

43:52.360 --> 43:53.500
But the human system

43:53.500 --> 43:55.000
cannot tolerate the mess.

43:55.360 --> 43:56.520
Which leads us

43:56.520 --> 43:57.560
to the devastating

43:57.560 --> 43:58.980
final act of the text.

43:58.980 --> 44:04.880
The film executes

44:04.880 --> 44:06.580
a massive temporal jump.

44:07.060 --> 44:08.060
We leap forward

44:08.060 --> 44:09.080
over a century,

44:09.340 --> 44:10.580
and the entire optical

44:10.580 --> 44:11.640
and acoustic language

44:11.640 --> 44:12.260
of the movie

44:12.260 --> 44:13.480
violently shifts.

44:13.940 --> 44:14.960
All the overlapping

44:14.960 --> 44:16.500
whispers of the antechamber,

44:16.640 --> 44:17.740
the smell of the tavern,

44:17.900 --> 44:18.860
the chaotic wind

44:18.860 --> 44:20.040
blowing the soap bubbles,

44:20.260 --> 44:22.000
it is entirely wiped out.

44:22.000 --> 44:22.940
We are suddenly

44:22.940 --> 44:24.560
in a massive printing house

44:24.560 --> 44:25.340
in Amsterdam

44:25.340 --> 44:27.400
in the late 17th century.

44:27.960 --> 44:29.400
The lighting is cold,

44:29.960 --> 44:30.320
flat,

44:30.560 --> 44:31.160
and absolute.

44:31.780 --> 44:32.480
The environment

44:32.480 --> 44:34.060
is clinically clean.

44:34.660 --> 44:36.400
There is no ambiguity here.

44:36.840 --> 44:37.780
This is the realm

44:37.780 --> 44:38.540
of pure,

44:38.980 --> 44:39.640
organized,

44:39.800 --> 44:41.000
mechanical information.

44:41.620 --> 44:42.460
A woman carries

44:42.460 --> 44:43.460
a bundle of paper

44:43.460 --> 44:45.080
to a master compositor

44:45.080 --> 44:46.480
at a typesetting desk.

44:47.080 --> 44:49.380
It is Rorio's life's work.

44:49.880 --> 44:50.980
The physical manuscript

44:50.980 --> 44:51.880
is a mess

44:51.880 --> 44:53.180
of crossed-out lines,

44:53.340 --> 44:53.960
marginalia,

44:54.520 --> 44:55.060
inkblots

44:55.060 --> 44:55.880
from where his pens

44:55.880 --> 44:56.920
stopped in the dark,

44:57.140 --> 44:58.260
and contradictory

44:58.260 --> 44:59.520
accounts of his travels.

44:59.960 --> 45:01.680
It is the physical artifact

45:01.680 --> 45:03.780
of a complex human soul.

45:04.600 --> 45:06.120
And what does the compositor do?

45:06.440 --> 45:08.300
He treats this chaotic soul

45:08.300 --> 45:10.220
purely as a mechanical problem.

45:10.860 --> 45:12.180
He begins setting the text

45:12.180 --> 45:13.380
into cold,

45:13.620 --> 45:14.260
identical,

45:14.740 --> 45:16.240
interchangeable lead type.

45:16.480 --> 45:17.260
When he encounters

45:17.260 --> 45:18.040
a contradiction

45:18.040 --> 45:19.220
in the handwritten notes,

45:19.440 --> 45:20.280
two different dates

45:20.280 --> 45:21.200
for the same event,

45:21.720 --> 45:23.040
or a nuanced hesitation

45:23.040 --> 45:24.460
in Rorio's philosophy,

45:25.000 --> 45:26.640
he doesn't agonize over it.

45:26.840 --> 45:27.440
He doesn't hold

45:27.440 --> 45:28.620
the diet of Regensburg

45:28.620 --> 45:29.600
to find the truth.

45:30.020 --> 45:30.900
He simply makes

45:30.900 --> 45:32.440
a unilateral decision.

45:32.820 --> 45:33.840
He picks one version,

45:34.300 --> 45:35.140
sets it in lead,

45:35.420 --> 45:36.680
and physically tosses

45:36.680 --> 45:37.840
the alternative letters

45:37.840 --> 45:38.600
back into the

45:38.600 --> 45:39.540
wooden sorting case.

45:39.940 --> 45:41.340
He literally throws

45:41.340 --> 45:42.560
the variant history

45:42.560 --> 45:43.860
into the trash.

45:44.440 --> 45:46.260
The nuance is annihilated

45:46.260 --> 45:47.900
by the mechanical requirements

45:47.900 --> 45:48.920
of the printing press.

45:49.300 --> 45:50.320
The camera then moves

45:50.320 --> 45:51.240
to Rotterdam

45:51.240 --> 45:52.820
into the meticulously

45:52.820 --> 45:53.960
organized study

45:53.960 --> 45:54.880
of Pierre Bale.

45:55.420 --> 45:57.080
Bale was a massive figure

45:57.080 --> 45:57.660
in the history

45:57.660 --> 45:58.460
of information.

45:59.140 --> 45:59.720
He compiled

45:59.720 --> 46:00.420
the Dictionnaire

46:00.420 --> 46:01.760
Historique et Critique,

46:02.020 --> 46:02.700
which was essentially

46:02.700 --> 46:04.600
Wikipedia of the 17th century,

46:04.980 --> 46:06.840
an encyclopedic attempt

46:06.840 --> 46:08.220
to categorize

46:08.220 --> 46:09.560
all human knowledge

46:09.560 --> 46:11.000
into a stable,

46:11.440 --> 46:12.560
alphabetical format.

46:13.080 --> 46:13.840
Bale is sitting

46:13.840 --> 46:14.600
at his desk,

46:14.920 --> 46:15.980
compiling the entry

46:15.980 --> 46:17.060
for the letter R.

46:17.760 --> 46:19.260
He has three different

46:19.260 --> 46:21.100
conflicting historical sources

46:21.100 --> 46:22.720
about Girolamo Rorario

46:22.720 --> 46:23.580
in front of him,

46:24.140 --> 46:25.240
sources written by people

46:25.240 --> 46:26.320
who live through the mud

46:26.320 --> 46:27.160
and the chaos.

46:27.480 --> 46:29.060
Bale scans them in seconds.

46:29.600 --> 46:30.520
He is the ultimate

46:30.520 --> 46:31.780
administrative filter.

46:32.460 --> 46:33.520
He is looking for data

46:33.520 --> 46:35.280
that fits the rigid architecture

46:35.280 --> 46:36.380
of an encyclopedia.

46:36.860 --> 46:38.000
If a detail is

46:38.000 --> 46:39.660
epistemologically unstable,

46:40.020 --> 46:41.140
if it contradicts

46:41.140 --> 46:42.000
another source,

46:42.180 --> 46:43.400
or if it simply takes up

46:43.400 --> 46:44.540
too much physical space

46:44.540 --> 46:45.220
on the page,

46:45.580 --> 46:46.560
he performs an act

46:46.560 --> 46:47.620
of epistemic violence.

46:47.620 --> 46:48.980
He simply pushes

46:48.980 --> 46:49.620
the document

46:49.620 --> 46:50.760
to the edge of his desk.

46:50.980 --> 46:51.760
He discards it.

46:52.100 --> 46:52.720
He strips away

46:52.720 --> 46:53.700
the hesitations,

46:54.160 --> 46:54.740
the fear,

46:55.120 --> 46:56.380
the animal immediacy,

46:56.640 --> 46:57.880
and this leads

46:57.880 --> 46:59.700
to the absolute gut punch

46:59.700 --> 47:00.620
of Fliction's screenplay.

47:01.380 --> 47:02.620
Rorario's entire universe,

47:03.660 --> 47:06.060
the horrifying 1.5 seconds

47:06.060 --> 47:07.180
of the street theater,

47:07.680 --> 47:08.620
the translator destroying

47:09.180 --> 47:09.760
a treaty,

47:10.140 --> 47:11.080
the dog slipping

47:11.080 --> 47:11.920
through the carts,

47:11.920 --> 47:13.600
the terror of hearing

47:13.600 --> 47:14.580
his relative's voice

47:14.580 --> 47:15.600
as pure noise,

47:15.940 --> 47:17.680
the horse saving his life

47:17.680 --> 47:18.300
at the bridge,

47:18.420 --> 47:19.060
all of it.

47:19.500 --> 47:21.240
It is fed into Bale's machine

47:21.240 --> 47:22.520
and it is compressed down

47:22.520 --> 47:24.840
into exactly 11 lines of text.

47:25.140 --> 47:25.940
11 lines.

47:26.200 --> 47:27.800
Fliction's concluding narration

47:27.800 --> 47:29.220
delivers the philosophical

47:29.220 --> 47:30.040
kill shot.

47:30.440 --> 47:31.320
The text reads,

47:31.320 --> 47:33.040
It is within its own

47:33.040 --> 47:34.060
constraints set

47:34.060 --> 47:35.580
a successful object.

47:35.900 --> 47:37.020
The entry is legible.

47:37.420 --> 47:38.640
The entry is stable.

47:39.240 --> 47:40.260
Nothing in the entry

47:40.260 --> 47:41.120
indicates that

47:41.120 --> 47:42.140
anything is missing.

47:42.600 --> 47:43.660
Nothing in the entry

47:43.660 --> 47:44.320
indicates that

47:44.320 --> 47:45.100
anything is missing.

47:45.300 --> 47:45.440
Yeah,

47:45.500 --> 47:46.720
the philosophical weight

47:46.720 --> 47:47.320
of that ending

47:47.320 --> 47:48.580
is just massive.

47:49.100 --> 47:50.260
The sheer horror

47:50.260 --> 47:51.340
of that sentence,

47:52.000 --> 47:52.620
because we,

47:52.780 --> 47:53.500
having lived through

47:53.500 --> 47:54.440
the event history

47:54.440 --> 47:55.280
with Rorario,

47:55.700 --> 47:57.200
know that everything

47:57.200 --> 47:58.100
is missing.

47:58.100 --> 47:59.980
The entire bleeding,

48:00.220 --> 48:01.280
breathing reality

48:01.280 --> 48:01.900
of life

48:01.900 --> 48:03.540
has been scrubbed away

48:03.540 --> 48:05.240
to create a clean,

48:05.520 --> 48:06.800
easy-to-read paragraph.

48:07.200 --> 48:08.520
History isn't a record

48:08.520 --> 48:09.180
of the truth.

48:09.680 --> 48:10.500
History is just

48:10.500 --> 48:11.760
the sterile residue

48:11.760 --> 48:13.220
of what managed

48:13.220 --> 48:13.860
to survive

48:13.860 --> 48:14.920
the violent compression

48:14.920 --> 48:16.020
of the filing cabinet.

48:16.620 --> 48:17.640
It's the lead type

48:17.640 --> 48:18.900
that didn't get thrown away.

48:19.340 --> 48:20.240
If we pull

48:20.240 --> 48:21.300
all of this together,

48:21.520 --> 48:22.140
City of Brutes

48:22.140 --> 48:22.760
is demanding

48:22.760 --> 48:24.380
a total re-evaluation

48:24.380 --> 48:25.820
of how we view

48:25.820 --> 48:26.980
our own intellect.

48:26.980 --> 48:28.120
It posits that

48:28.120 --> 48:29.020
animals are not

48:29.020 --> 48:30.720
lesser mechanical beasts.

48:31.520 --> 48:32.440
They are the absolute

48:32.440 --> 48:34.220
masters of the present tense.

48:34.760 --> 48:35.780
They exist in a state

48:35.780 --> 48:36.420
of grace,

48:36.920 --> 48:38.580
maintaining a zero-latency

48:38.580 --> 48:40.040
dialogue with the

48:40.040 --> 48:40.980
physical universe.

48:41.340 --> 48:41.700
Humans,

48:41.960 --> 48:42.700
on the other hand,

48:42.760 --> 48:43.840
are tragic creatures.

48:44.380 --> 48:44.980
We are trapped

48:44.980 --> 48:46.100
in the agonizing

48:46.100 --> 48:47.400
lag of our own genius.

48:47.900 --> 48:48.680
We build maps,

48:49.100 --> 48:50.200
we write dictionaries,

48:50.400 --> 48:50.980
we invent bureaucracies,

48:51.840 --> 48:52.620
and then we become

48:52.620 --> 48:53.680
completely lost

48:53.680 --> 48:54.200
within them.

48:54.440 --> 48:55.480
We spend our lives

48:55.480 --> 48:56.660
desperately trying

48:56.660 --> 48:58.060
to force the chaotic,

48:58.500 --> 48:59.760
unresolvable truth

48:59.760 --> 49:00.940
of the physical world

49:00.940 --> 49:02.300
into the clean,

49:02.520 --> 49:03.260
false certainty

49:03.260 --> 49:04.800
of an eleven-line entry.

49:05.160 --> 49:05.760
Think about

49:05.760 --> 49:07.240
the blinking cursor again.

49:07.800 --> 49:08.260
Think about

49:08.260 --> 49:09.100
your own life

49:09.100 --> 49:10.100
right now today.

49:10.620 --> 49:11.480
The chaotic,

49:11.820 --> 49:12.520
exhausting,

49:12.740 --> 49:13.740
beautiful mess

49:13.740 --> 49:15.180
of your daily experiences,

49:15.400 --> 49:16.360
your hesitations.

49:17.000 --> 49:18.100
The times you've

49:18.100 --> 49:19.040
sat in a meeting

49:19.040 --> 49:19.900
where everyone

49:19.900 --> 49:21.460
is speaking corporate jargon,

49:21.540 --> 49:22.040
but nothing

49:22.040 --> 49:23.400
is actually being said.

49:23.400 --> 49:24.200
or the times

49:24.200 --> 49:24.640
you've felt

49:24.640 --> 49:26.200
the agonizing lag

49:26.200 --> 49:27.640
between what you feel

49:27.640 --> 49:28.400
and what you can

49:28.400 --> 49:29.360
actually express.

49:29.360 --> 49:30.420
But also,

49:30.700 --> 49:31.320
think about your

49:31.320 --> 49:32.100
perfect little

49:32.100 --> 49:33.400
animal moments.

49:33.920 --> 49:34.480
The moments

49:34.480 --> 49:35.260
where you were just

49:35.260 --> 49:36.260
acting,

49:36.580 --> 49:37.560
playing a sport,

49:37.900 --> 49:39.380
dodging a falling glass,

49:39.580 --> 49:40.800
laughing without thinking,

49:41.600 --> 49:42.360
just existing

49:42.360 --> 49:43.460
in the physical world

49:43.460 --> 49:44.340
without narrating

49:44.340 --> 49:45.080
it to yourself.

49:45.880 --> 49:46.500
Someday,

49:46.840 --> 49:47.580
all of this,

49:47.800 --> 49:48.460
your entire

49:48.460 --> 49:49.340
sprawling,

49:49.600 --> 49:50.620
complex life

49:50.620 --> 49:51.720
will be subjected

49:51.720 --> 49:52.740
to that exact

49:52.740 --> 49:54.220
same compression algorithm.

49:54.820 --> 49:55.820
It'll be flattened down

49:55.820 --> 49:56.900
to a few bullet points

49:56.900 --> 49:57.460
on a resume

49:57.460 --> 49:58.740
or a short,

49:58.860 --> 49:59.840
sanitized anecdote

49:59.840 --> 50:00.860
told by a relative

50:00.860 --> 50:01.760
who only remembers

50:01.760 --> 50:02.480
half the story.

50:03.200 --> 50:04.380
An 11-line entry.

50:04.700 --> 50:05.880
But the fact that

50:05.880 --> 50:07.420
history flattens us,

50:07.480 --> 50:08.440
the fact that the system

50:08.440 --> 50:09.680
only reads the header

50:09.680 --> 50:10.360
of the file

50:10.360 --> 50:12.120
and misses the brilliant,

50:12.380 --> 50:12.960
corrupted,

50:13.600 --> 50:14.940
chaotic code inside,

50:15.280 --> 50:16.060
doesn't mean

50:16.060 --> 50:17.160
the mess isn't real.

50:17.460 --> 50:18.680
The mess is the only place

50:18.680 --> 50:20.360
where actual living happens.

50:20.960 --> 50:21.820
So the next time

50:21.820 --> 50:22.540
you find yourself

50:22.540 --> 50:23.800
stuck at a narrow gate,

50:24.360 --> 50:25.140
gridlocked,

50:25.160 --> 50:26.640
and ridiculous negotiation

50:26.640 --> 50:27.520
over the arbitrary

50:27.520 --> 50:28.380
rules of life,

50:28.800 --> 50:29.920
endlessly debating

50:29.920 --> 50:30.920
who should back up

50:30.920 --> 50:31.900
and who should move forward,

50:32.300 --> 50:33.380
stopped looking at the map.

50:33.960 --> 50:34.500
Ask yourself,

50:34.580 --> 50:35.660
could you drop the script?

50:35.880 --> 50:37.000
Could you just slip

50:37.000 --> 50:37.740
through the gap

50:37.740 --> 50:38.580
like the dog?

50:39.280 --> 50:40.260
Thank you for joining us

50:40.260 --> 50:41.240
on this deep dive

50:41.240 --> 50:42.120
into the sources.

50:42.420 --> 50:43.580
Keep questioning the map

50:43.580 --> 50:44.580
and we'll see you next time.

